00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:16,400
so the best perplexity you can have is one.

221
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:21,892
If you really have no idea, you basically predict with one divided by size of vocabulary.

222
00:20:22,320 --> 00:20:26,308
and then you do simple math and you basically get perplexity of size of vocabulary.

223
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:32,228
so the intuition of perplexity is that it's basically the number of tokens that your model is kind of hesitating between.

